2. FFmpeg (bundled binary, LGPL)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Evoice installers include an FFmpeg executable built WITHOUT --enable-gpl and
WITHOUT --enable-nonfree, so it is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public
License, version 2.1 or later (https://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl-2.1.html).
The macOS build also statically links LAME (libmp3lame, LGPL).

- Windows: prebuilt LGPL build from https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds
  (scripts: apps/desktop/scripts/fetch-ffmpeg.mjs)
- macOS (Apple Silicon and Intel): built from the official FFmpeg source release
  with apps/desktop/scripts/build-ffmpeg-mac.sh (FFmpeg 8.0.1, LAME, LGPL
  configuration only)
- FFmpeg source code: https://ffmpeg.org/download.html
  (the exact FFmpeg release used for macOS is set in build-ffmpeg-mac.sh)
- FFmpeg is a trademark of Fabrice Bellard, originator of the FFmpeg project.

You may replace the bundled FFmpeg: Evoice uses the ffmpeg executable found in
the "ffmpeg" folder next to the app, and falls back to ffmpeg in your PATH.

